{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-proverbs-020",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 20,
  "title": "Proverbs 20",
  "display_title": "Proverbs 20",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "proverbs",
  "book": "Proverbs",
  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 20,
  "sortOrder": 20020,
  "verseCount": 30,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Wine is a mocker, strong drink is raging: and whosoever is deceived thereby is not wise.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "The fear of a king is as the roaring of a lion: whoso provoketh him to anger sinneth against his own soul.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "It is an honour for a man to cease from strife: but every fool will be meddling.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "The sluggard will not plow by reason of the cold; therefore shall he beg in harvest, and have nothing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Counsel in the heart of man is like deep water; but a man of understanding will draw it out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Most men will proclaim every one his own goodness: but a faithful man who can find?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "The just man walketh in his integrity: his children are blessed after him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "A king that sitteth in the throne of judgment scattereth away all evil with his eyes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Who can say, I have made my heart clean, I am pure from my sin?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Divers weights, and divers measures, both of them are alike abomination to the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Even a child is known by his doings, whether his work be pure, and whether it be right.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, the LORD hath made even both of them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Love not sleep, lest thou come to poverty; open thine eyes, and thou shalt be satisfied with bread.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "It is naught, it is naught, saith the buyer: but when he is gone his way, then he boasteth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "There is gold, and a multitude of rubies: but the lips of knowledge are a precious jewel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Take his garment that is surety for a stranger: and take a pledge of him for a strange woman.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Bread of deceit is sweet to a man; but afterwards his mouth shall be filled with gravel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Every purpose is established by counsel: and with good advice make war.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "He that goeth about as a talebearer revealeth secrets: therefore meddle not with him that flattereth with his lips.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Whoso curseth his father or his mother, his lamp shall be put out in obscure darkness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "An inheritance may be gotten hastily at the beginning; but the end thereof shall not be blessed.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Say not thou, I will recompense evil; but wait on the LORD, and he shall save thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Divers weights are an abomination unto the LORD; and a false balance is not good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Man’s goings are of the LORD; how can a man then understand his own way?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "It is a snare to the man who devoureth that which is holy, and after vows to make enquiry.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "A wise king scattereth the wicked, and bringeth the wheel over them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "The spirit of man is the candle of the LORD, searching all the inward parts of the belly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Mercy and truth preserve the king: and his throne is upholden by mercy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "The glory of young men is their strength: and the beauty of old men is the grey head.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:20:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "The blueness of a wound cleanseth away evil: so do stripes the inward parts of the belly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 20:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:20:30"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
